#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""my-otr -- search, download and decode OTR recordings.

Searches otr.datenkeller.net, downloads with aria2c, and decodes both of
onlinetvrecorder.com's formats itself: `.otr2` (since 2026) and `.otrkey`
(before). `my-otr --help` says how to drive it.

One file, in this order:
  1. bootstrap   -- the venv ~/.python.venv/my-otr (stdlib only up to here)
  2. output, errors, config
  3. recordings: names, qualities, the search filter, the copies already here
  4. HTTP, otr.datenkeller.net, aria2c
  5. the OTR protocol -- our own code; OTR's decoder is only the reference it
     was written from (`my-otr update-check <ZIP>` lists what a release changed)
  6. commands, main, --run-tests
"""

